      "content_summary": "Troubleshooting steps for Attribution Engine and Subscription Manager failures caused by third-party API rate limits or vendor outages.",
      "content_body": "1. Check the vendor's status page for active incidents regarding rate limiting or service degradation. 2. Verify if the error logs show 429 Too Many Requests or timeout signals from the upstream dependency. 3. Implement or adjust existing backoff and retry logic within the Attribution Engine to handle transient failures gracefully. 4. Engage the third-party vendor to request a temporary rate limit increase if the issue persists. 5. For Subscription Manager, ensure fallback mechanisms are active to prevent user-facing billing interruptions during vendor downtime."
